ested mathematical conditional, not as execution certification.\",\"checks\":{\"inputs\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"All cited N inputs are declared packet inputs, with compatible r instantiation. N001 supplies integrability and the stated measurable-space/Lebesgue context; N002 supplies differentiability and the derivative-integral identity; N003 supplies the derivative formula; N004 supplies the pointwise zero identity. M015 is an explicitly stated permitted input, treated conditionally as requested.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs/0/statement\",\"/inputs/1/statement\",\"/inputs/2/statement\",\"/inputs/3/statement\",\"/inputs/4/statement\",\"/inference/argument/0\",\"/inference/argument/1\"]},\"argument\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"For arbitrary positive r, N003 identifies E′(r) with twice the whole-space integral of the displayed integrand. N004 makes the integrand zero at every x. Applying M015 to that zero real-valued function yields integral zero, and the permitted scalar calculation gives E′(r)=0. N001 and N002 give the integrability and differentiability clauses. No additional analysis theorem is needed.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/applications/0\"]},\"dependency_accounting\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Each listed input has an identifiable role: N001 supports integrability and context, N002 supports differentiability and derivative-integral identity, N003 supplies the derivative formula, N004 supplies the zero integrand, and M015 evaluates its integral. No additional nontrivial theorem is hidden in the proof. N001's extra compact-support and continuity clauses are unused but do not undermine the argument.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/inputs\",\"/inference/argument/0\",\"/inference/argument/1\",\"/inference/applications/0\"]},\"output\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The argument proves all three clauses of P for arbitrary r>0: integrability and differentiability come from N001/N002, and the derivative-zero clause follows from the second step. The universal quantifier is closed by the stated forall_introduction rule.\",\"locations\":[\"/output/statement\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/rules\"]},\"scope\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"r is declared arbitrary positive and remains in scope through both steps; forall_introduction closes it. There are no temporary assumptions, existential witnesses, or escaping facts. The h notation is confined to S002; its missing declaration inventory is recorded under object_closure, not a scope error.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/locals/0\",\"/inference/argument/0\",\"/inference/argument/1\",\"/inference/rules\"]},\"applicability\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"M015 is applied to X=ℝⁿ with the stated Borel measurable space, Lebesgue measure, and V=ℝ. Its stated structural conditions are identified in the application, and N004 establishes that the integrand is identically zero. The application conclusion is exactly that integral equals zero.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs/4/statement\",\"/inference/applications/0/bindings\",\"/inference/applications/0/hypothesis_checks\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inputs/0/statement\"]},\"statement_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The input and target statements explicitly state the mathematical claims used and the target claims, with their quantifiers and domains. D002 specifies the partial-integral convention; N002 supplies the needed integrability before E is used. The local h equation is written inline in S002 and is therefore intelligible despite its missing object inventory entry.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs/0/statement\",\"/inputs/1/statement\",\"/inputs/2/statement\",\"/inputs/3/statement\",\"/inputs/4/statement\",\"/definitions/1/definition\",\"/output/statement\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\"]},\"object_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"S002 actually uses h as a real-valued function of x, introduced by “where h(x)=...”. There is no h declaration in the local-declaration inventory, and h is absent from S002's objects list. The inline equation conveys its intended definition, so this is a missing formal object/declaration accounting entry rather than an unsupported inference.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/locals\",\"/inference/argument/1/objects\"]},\"dependency_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Reverse-checking the prose, all substantive factual claims trace to listed inputs: the derivative identity to N002/N003, pointwise vanishing to N004, integral evaluation to M015, and integrability to N001/N002. The inline definition of h is notation for the displayed integrand, not an additional theorem. No ancestor proof or source proof is used.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/inputs\",\"/inference/applications/0\"]},\"packet_replay\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"On the requested mathematical conditional—given the externally checked packet/carrier input boundary—the packet alone contains the statements and argument sufficient to derive P, as explained above. This is the packet read in this context and no other mathematical task material was read. This PASS does not certify execution isolation, carrier identity, or runtime attestation; those are outside this mathematical judgment. The object-inventory defect is a recorded structural closure issue, not missing mathematical content or an unsupported implication.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs\",\"/definitions\",\"/output/statement\",\"/inference/argument\",\"/inference/applications\"]}},\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"F001\",\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"location\":\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"explanation\":\"S002 introduces and uses h(x) but the inference has no corresponding local declaration; h is also omitted from the step's object inventory. The inline equation makes the notation mathematically interpretable, but Audit A object closure requires actual occurrences to map to a legitimate recorded declaration. This is the first defect and does not identify a false or unsupported mathematical implication.\"}]}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read an explicitly frozen task document by ID; no other local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report exact status, location, explanation, basis, partial_progress. SUBSTANTIVE_GAP or SUSPECTED_GAP stops for an actual unsupported mathematical implication; give its premises, conclusion and mathematical grounds. SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE or INPUT_CONFLICT stops for a real source-access/original-input obstacle. Ordinary unfinished d